// DeliveryReceipt is the server telling a sending user's devices that
// recipient devices acknowledged envelopes they sent: the E2EE counterpart
// of the plaintext system's DELIVERED pointer, and the one receipt the
// server can issue on its own, since it can see acknowledgements. READ
// receipts are between clients, inside the encrypted channel
// (content.proto ReceiptMessage), and this message mirrors that one's
// shape: a list of parties, each with the messages it concerns. There the
// party is an author and the message a MessageId; here the party is an
// acknowledging device and the message a client_ts, the one handle the
// server can see. The chat is the enclosing Envelope's chat_id, as it is
// for a ReceiptMessage.
