// acknowledged, whatever its client_ts, because the server has no order
// over a device's sends it can promise is complete (a recipient
// acknowledges only what it stored, and re-receives the rest later). The
// server folds: every acknowledgement one device makes in one call, and
// acknowledgements of the same sends that arrive within a short window,
// become one receipt per sender device rather than one envelope each, so a
// device draining a day's messages earns each sender one receipt, and a
// large group's acknowledgements of a message arrive as a few receipts,
// not one per member device. A send already reported may appear again
// after a retry; clients treat the set as monotonic and aggregate per
// user. Issued for PREKEY_MESSAGE, CIPHERTEXT and SENDER_KEY_MESSAGE
// envelopes; never for PLAINTEXT_CONTENT, never for an envelope delivered
